font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><strong>Course Description:</strong><br><em>Theory and Practice of Infectious Disease Nursing</em> is a highly specialized course evolved from the broader discipline of infectious disease nursing. It focuses on the commonalities, characteristics, and patterns of infectious diseases, including their transmission and epidemiological processes, prevention and control strategies, nursing assessment and interventions, and specific management considerations in infectious disease care. The applied section introduces the clinical features, epidemiological characteristics, diagnosis, prevention, and nursing essentials of prevalent and high-incidence infectious diseases in China.</p>
<p>Through theoretical study, students will acquire foundational knowledge and clinical skills in managing common infectious diseases, apply the nursing process throughout their practice, and deliver comprehensive patient care. Moreover, the course aims to help students develop a rational and empathetic understanding of infectious diseases, eliminate fear and stigma, and appreciate the spirit of scientific inquiry and medical professionalism demonstrated by predecessors. Students are expected to recognize the significance of infectious disease prevention and control and actively engage in relevant nursing work.</p>
<p>This course is designed for undergraduate nursing students specializing in public health nursing and is divided into two parts:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Part I: Theory and Practice of Infectious Disease Nursing (I)</strong> (16 hours) focuses on:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The etiology, epidemiology, clinical manifestations, laboratory diagnosis, treatment, and nursing care of emerging infectious diseases, with an emphasis on prevention and clinical nursing management—aligned with the competencies needed in public health nursing;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Social factors contributing to emerging infectious diseases;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>New challenges related to re-emerging infectious diseases.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Part II: Theory and Practice of Infectious Disease Nursing (II)</strong> (16 hours) focuses on:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Emergency management of public health outbreaks;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Disinfection and isolation in infectious disease wards;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Response to infectious disease outbreaks at borders and in communities;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Hospital-acquired infection and antimicrobial resistance control;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Case management and follow-up of patients with chronic infectious diseases.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
